  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 51. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. 雑貨 — 日々の暮らしで使ういろいろな小物。\n2. 雑草 — 人が育てていない所などに自然に生える草。\n3. 仕上がり — 作った物などが完成したときの様子。\n4. 仕上げ — 完成させるために最後に整えること。\n5. シアター — 映画や演劇などを見るための施設。\n6. 詩歌 — 詩や短歌など。\n7. 仕入れ — 売るための商品や材料を買い入れること。\n8. シェア — 一つのものを分け合ったり共同で使ったりすること。\n9. シェフ — 西洋料理などの料理長。\n10. 塩味 — 塩によるしょっぱい味。\n11. 仕掛け — ある働きをするように工夫した仕組み。\n12. 仕方 — 物事を行う方法。\n13. 市街地 — 家や店などが集まった町の区域。\n14. 敷居 — 戸をはめるために床の境に設ける横木など。\n15. 色彩 — いろいろな色やその取り合わせ。\n16. 色紙 — 書や絵をかくための四角い厚紙。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\nDo not add numerical claims, prices, quantities, currency denominations, calorie values or stroke-order numbers unless explicitly required by the target word. Mathematical concepts should have neutral concrete examples without unverified numeric diagrams.\n",
